  "observations": [
    "The previous 384-square merchandise render shows a genuine three-quarter square backless stool: two plank seams, a honey-yellow seat with visible front/right thickness, splayed brown legs, and distinct lower stretchers/open gaps. It has hard faceted perimeter bands and darker supports than the exact approved warm-soft world source.",
    "At 96 and 66 full-frame pixels the previous goods snapshot still reads as a stool with a top plane and separable legs. The supplement must retain this genuine three-dimensional presentation and the camera-controlled scale, rather than inserting a straight-on registered world sprite.",
    "The fixed imagegen target is the same original world-style reference. Its broad warm highlights, inset seam vocabulary and soft finish inform style; its padded silhouette, shifted framing and stray alpha glow do not authorize changing the approved model or merchandise camera.",
    "Read-only native Blender inspection of the exact approved source found the named export scene, eleven stool meshes, an identity root transform at S0, warm honey/brown/stretcher/groove materials, a centered overhead plus eight equal ring fills, Cycles, Standard view/exposure0/gamma1 and compositing disabled. No external file images or linked libraries are present. Root normalization is not needed for this inspected source.",
    "Actual existing Godot native captures show four first-page Layout cards (Belt, Stool, Plant, Crate), dynamic stock labels 6/4/2/2 left, a one-card Barrel last page with1 left and reversed disabled page boundary, and a muted disabled Floor preview. Beige/ivory card surfaces, indigo curtains, bare paging carets and the wooden dock form the existing context.",
    "Read the current production ItemPreview code: goods use the 384-square atlas region uniformly fit into the existing preview control; Layout has four cards and no raster occupied-pixel crop for goods. Dynamic labels and count/disabled logic are native controls. These surfaces and logic are outside the supplement edit scope."
  ],
